WEBVTT

00:15.000 --> 00:16.160
[church bells ringing]

00:20.120 --> 00:21.560
Good morning, sisters.

00:25.960 --> 00:27.040
Let us pray.

00:29.560 --> 00:30.880
[engine revving]

00:40.920 --> 00:42.680
Our Father, who art in heaven...

00:46.280 --> 00:48.280
[rock song playing]

00:53.560 --> 00:55.320
...but deliver us from evil.

01:02.840 --> 01:05.120
[Mother Superior] For thine is
the kingdom, the power...

01:05.200 --> 01:06.040
[coughs]

01:06.120 --> 01:08.760
...forever and ever. Amen.

01:18.520 --> 01:20.840
[Mother Superior] You wanted
to speak to us, Mr Shelby?

01:20.920 --> 01:22.200
Yep.

01:22.280 --> 01:24.120
-All of us?
-Yep.

01:24.200 --> 01:26.880
At 6:30 in the morning?

01:26.960 --> 01:27.800
[Tommy] Yes.

01:31.520 --> 01:32.920
We don't smoke in here.

01:33.000 --> 01:34.120
Well, I fucking do.

01:35.760 --> 01:36.960
Nor do we use language.

01:37.920 --> 01:39.880
Nor do we find fault in the innocent.

01:40.640 --> 01:41.800
Yet, you do.

01:42.800 --> 01:44.200
You fucking do.

01:49.920 --> 01:52.000
May I ask what this meeting is about?

01:52.080 --> 01:55.440
The Grace Shelby Foundation
is the biggest single source of funding

01:55.520 --> 01:56.760
for this charitable institution

01:56.840 --> 01:59.960
devoted to the care of the orphaned girls
of South Birmingham, yeah?

02:01.120 --> 02:02.400
For which we give thanks.

02:02.960 --> 02:03.840
Uh-huh.

02:05.520 --> 02:09.240
I have a temper similar to the one
described in that report.

02:09.320 --> 02:12.240
Yet, unlike you,
I wait until I'm matched in size.

02:13.039 --> 02:14.320
Whose report?

02:16.160 --> 02:17.920
The testimony of children.

02:22.200 --> 02:23.440
Who have they spoken to?

02:25.240 --> 02:27.400
You'd have them only speak to God.

02:27.480 --> 02:28.760
[Mother Superior] God be their witness.

02:28.840 --> 02:31.520
There is God,
and there are the Peaky Blinders.

02:32.120 --> 02:33.960
This is Sparkhill, we're in Small Heath.

02:34.520 --> 02:36.840
We're much, much closer at hand than God.

02:36.920 --> 02:39.640
And we have heard terrible things.

02:40.160 --> 02:44.160
We have, in this place,
children of the worst sort.

02:44.240 --> 02:45.960
They lie as easily as breathe.

02:46.040 --> 02:47.400
[Polly] You had a child half black.

02:47.480 --> 02:49.360
You made her wash with a different soap.

02:52.640 --> 02:55.800
Mr Shelby, your own sins are legend.

02:55.880 --> 02:57.200
[Tommy] Our sins.

03:00.920 --> 03:04.240
Our sins against the beating of children

03:04.320 --> 03:07.440
with bricks and hoses.

03:07.520 --> 03:08.720
Our sins...

03:15.480 --> 03:16.640
Our sins...

03:22.160 --> 03:25.560
against the black child who hanged herself
for fear of your temper.

03:29.000 --> 03:30.640
-[Mother Superior] I do not see how--
-You do not see...

03:35.920 --> 03:37.320
Now put 'em on.

03:39.520 --> 03:40.960
Put 'em on your face

03:41.600 --> 03:43.560
or it'll be your eyes that are broken.

03:45.040 --> 03:47.840
And please don't imagine
that I won't use this minute to do it

03:47.920 --> 03:52.280
or that I am afraid of your prayers
or your crosses.

04:15.640 --> 04:17.600
You see the world broken.

04:18.760 --> 04:20.720
Like those beaten children will.

04:22.399 --> 04:23.600
[Tommy] Now look at me.

04:25.560 --> 04:26.640
Look at me.

04:28.520 --> 04:30.080
[breathes deeply]

04:32.120 --> 04:33.520
Look at me!

04:36.280 --> 04:37.720
Funding withdrawn.

04:42.120 --> 04:44.320
All children to be
taken into our own institutions.

04:44.400 --> 04:46.480
You have no say in where the children--

04:46.560 --> 04:48.000
[Polly] If I come for you,

04:48.080 --> 04:50.920
and I still might yet decide
to come for you,

04:51.640 --> 04:53.040
I will wear high heels

04:53.120 --> 04:55.560
so you can hear my approach
on the cobblestones

04:55.640 --> 04:57.440
and have time to repent.

04:58.520 --> 05:00.200
[church bells ringing]

05:04.040 --> 05:06.360
You listen for my footsteps.

05:22.960 --> 05:24.480
Happy birthday, Pol.

05:26.920 --> 05:29.000
You grow grand in the horse shit, Pol.

05:30.960 --> 05:32.400
Curly, pour some beer, eh?

05:35.720 --> 05:37.560
The train to London leaves in an hour.

05:38.080 --> 05:41.000
Arthur, Michael, you're coming with me.

05:41.080 --> 05:43.720
Tommy, I have to take Gina
to the hospital today.

05:44.840 --> 05:49.840
A week ago, one of our most trusted men
was killed by Jimmy McCavern.

05:50.880 --> 05:52.560
The man we're going to speak to in London

05:52.640 --> 05:54.600
is establishing a relationship
with Jimmy McCavern.

05:54.680 --> 05:56.480
So, cancel your appointments,

05:56.560 --> 05:58.480
and Ada can take Gina to the hospital.

05:58.560 --> 06:00.080
'Cause that's what women do.

06:00.160 --> 06:01.000
[scoffs]

06:02.160 --> 06:04.960
Clean that shit off your shoes
before you get in me car, eh?

06:07.480 --> 06:10.400
Michael, they will give it and give it
until your case is proven,

06:10.480 --> 06:11.440
and then they'll take it.

06:11.520 --> 06:14.400
From you, but mainly from me.

06:14.480 --> 06:17.720
Polly, you go to the hospital
and speak to Aberama Gold.

06:18.480 --> 06:22.880
You tell him there is a strategy in place
to avenge the death of his son,

06:22.960 --> 06:25.440
so not to do anything rash.
And take with you

06:25.520 --> 06:28.000
the heartfelt condolences
of the whole family.

06:28.080 --> 06:29.200
Why me?

06:30.640 --> 06:34.640
Because Aberama Gold is in love with you.
He even got an haircut.

06:34.720 --> 06:38.000
And the smell of your perfume
might help ease his pain.

06:38.080 --> 06:40.600
Tommy, I'm 45 years old today.

06:40.680 --> 06:43.280
Forty-five years old
and still breaking hearts, eh?

06:43.360 --> 06:44.840
-[Arthur] Yeah.
-To Polly.

06:44.920 --> 06:46.360
-Polly Gray. Hmm?
-Right.

06:46.440 --> 06:47.400
Polly.

06:47.480 --> 06:48.880
Happy birthday, Pol, yeah.

06:49.480 --> 06:52.960
Curly, organise a wagon
to take Bonnie Gold's soul to heaven.

06:53.640 --> 06:57.920
Isiah, fetch his boxing gloves
from the gym to burn with his body.

06:58.640 --> 07:02.200
Michael, turn the Bentley around.
We have a train to catch.

07:02.280 --> 07:03.120
[chuckling]

07:04.680 --> 07:07.240
And don't forget to wipe
that shit off your shoes, eh?

07:11.440 --> 07:13.520
Just start up the car and drive.

07:14.600 --> 07:18.120
♪ There ain't no grave ♪ 

07:18.200 --> 07:21.480
♪ Can hold my body down ♪

07:21.560 --> 07:24.880
♪ There ain't no grave ♪

07:24.960 --> 07:28.160
♪ Can hold my body down ♪

07:32.920 --> 07:34.640
[Michael] So, what's the strategy?

07:35.400 --> 07:38.200
You can smile. And you, don't smile.

07:38.960 --> 07:42.360
♪ There ain't no grave ♪

07:42.440 --> 07:44.920
♪ Can hold my body down ♪

07:45.000 --> 07:46.000
Nice.

07:47.080 --> 07:48.320
Very nice, Tom.

07:48.400 --> 07:49.240
Hmm.

07:50.640 --> 07:53.920
Although, I must say, I thought
your office would be bigger than this.

07:54.000 --> 07:54.920
It will be.

07:55.000 --> 07:58.280
Michael, you sit.
Arthur, you stand by the window.

08:08.280 --> 08:10.360
So, who we meetin'?

08:11.040 --> 08:13.080
[Tommy] The man we're about to meet

08:13.160 --> 08:15.360
is the minister
for the Duchy of Lancaster.

08:15.440 --> 08:19.400
He is also deputy
to the Chancellor of the Exchequer

08:19.480 --> 08:23.160
and Cabinet adviser
to the Prime Minister of Great Britain.

08:25.320 --> 08:27.000
You've both met bad men before.

08:29.560 --> 08:32.080
The man we're about to meet is the devil.

08:33.360 --> 08:34.320
[phone ringing]

08:37.440 --> 08:39.559
Yep. Send him in.

08:41.880 --> 08:43.480
[exhales heavily]

09:10.040 --> 09:12.600
I never seem to get to meet you
without your family.

09:18.560 --> 09:21.240
I understand you know a man
called Jimmy McCavern.

09:27.240 --> 09:28.640
May I take a cigarette?

09:30.160 --> 09:31.200
Please.

09:51.880 --> 09:53.720
Who on earth is Jimmy McCavern?

09:55.360 --> 09:56.880
Over the last 12 months,

09:56.960 --> 09:59.840
you've been making approaches
to various men across the country

10:00.640 --> 10:05.080
who you think might be able to
help you in your cause.

10:05.640 --> 10:07.200
McCavern is one of these men.

10:08.000 --> 10:10.040
He runs the East Glasgow shipyards.

10:10.120 --> 10:11.720
He killed an associate of mine.

10:13.800 --> 10:15.640
I want to know what your strategy is.

10:24.120 --> 10:26.480
That one's your brother, yes?

10:28.200 --> 10:29.200
[Michael] Yes.

10:29.800 --> 10:31.440
And I'm his business adviser.

10:33.480 --> 10:35.080
We would like to talk business.

10:37.080 --> 10:37.920
Michael.

10:39.320 --> 10:40.680
Michael Gray.

10:42.520 --> 10:45.640
You lost all your cousin's money
in America playing the fool.

10:45.720 --> 10:46.560
[tutting]

10:47.440 --> 10:52.080
A night club in Detroit
called the Gladiator is your regular.

10:52.160 --> 10:53.560
You lost the money...

10:54.520 --> 10:56.200
and found a wife there.

11:00.280 --> 11:04.320
And poor old Arthur Shelby,
standing there at the window,

11:04.400 --> 11:07.280
-is afraid his wife will never return.
-[wood creaking]

11:09.080 --> 11:11.920
My spies tell me she's been seen
with another man.

11:12.720 --> 11:14.880
Arthur... Arthur.

11:15.440 --> 11:17.280
[in Romani] His time will come.

11:17.360 --> 11:19.360
And... bingo.

11:20.200 --> 11:23.440
Twenty seconds in, and I have them
speaking their wog lingo.

11:24.600 --> 11:25.440
[sighs]

11:27.000 --> 11:29.120
Mr Shelby, I do have plans.

11:29.200 --> 11:32.440
I will have need of men like you.

11:33.800 --> 11:36.640
Except, of course,
there is no other man like you.

11:37.920 --> 11:41.040
You, in particular, I need.

11:42.280 --> 11:43.320
But please.

11:44.000 --> 11:46.640
Don't imagine I would
trouble myself with turf wars.

11:47.400 --> 11:48.840
You have many enemies.

11:49.520 --> 11:51.960
Shuffle the pack and pick another card.

11:59.600 --> 12:04.240
That investigation
of the dead journalist, the queer...

12:04.800 --> 12:06.400
I've made that go away.

12:08.480 --> 12:11.200
Read it and, er, come back to me.

12:12.280 --> 12:16.520
Next time, bring only an open mind
and a cigar to celebrate our union.

12:25.480 --> 12:26.320
[door opens]

12:28.720 --> 12:29.560
[door closes]

12:32.040 --> 12:33.120
[Tommy exhales]

12:36.600 --> 12:37.440
[clears throat]

12:58.400 --> 13:00.360
What the fuck was that all about, Tom?

13:02.160 --> 13:03.000
Fuck.

13:03.760 --> 13:04.720
Fuck.

13:08.560 --> 13:10.760
-[Arthur breathing heavily]
-[Tommy] Arthur!

13:11.800 --> 13:15.400
Do not let them get inside your head.

13:16.400 --> 13:18.760
That's exactly how these people work.

13:18.840 --> 13:20.840
Who the fuck are these people?

13:20.920 --> 13:21.760
Hmm?

13:22.920 --> 13:24.120
Who the fuck are they?

13:25.880 --> 13:26.720
[smacks lips]

13:27.480 --> 13:29.000
[sighs] I've just been invited...

13:29.080 --> 13:31.800
[clears throat]
...to become the deputy leader

13:32.760 --> 13:34.600
of a brand-new political party.

13:35.800 --> 13:36.640
[smacks lips]

13:37.160 --> 13:39.520
These people say they are the future.

13:40.040 --> 13:41.640
[Arthur breathing heavily]

13:51.520 --> 13:52.840
Do you want a drink?

13:52.920 --> 13:54.160
I've stopped.

14:01.160 --> 14:02.480
So, what have you decided?

14:03.720 --> 14:05.680
I've been talking to the Friends.

14:07.480 --> 14:09.000
What friends?

14:09.080 --> 14:12.320
Quakers. Friends who meet
at the Meeting House in Bournville.

14:13.280 --> 14:14.440
I'm staying in Bournville.

14:18.360 --> 14:19.800
[Lizzie] And what do they say?

14:19.880 --> 14:21.560
They say I have been led astray.

14:26.520 --> 14:29.880
If you've come to talk about redemption,
you're talking to the wrong person.

14:30.760 --> 14:32.680
I also went to a solicitor.

14:33.840 --> 14:37.040
They heard my name was Shelby,
and suddenly, they were too busy.

14:37.840 --> 14:41.160
To divorce a Shelby man,
you have to go to a solicitor in London.

14:42.480 --> 14:43.520
I found one.

14:44.040 --> 14:45.360
He said he'd represent me.

14:46.680 --> 14:48.000
But I put the phone down.

14:48.840 --> 14:50.120
Not through fear.

14:52.520 --> 14:54.880
I chose this life, it didn't choose me.

14:54.960 --> 14:56.760
Also, Lizzie, one of the Friends is a man.

14:58.960 --> 15:01.120
He listens to me when I talk.

15:03.240 --> 15:05.360
His wife died of the Spanish flu.

15:06.400 --> 15:07.480
He has a daughter.

15:07.560 --> 15:09.640
And you're considering
making this daughter an orphan.

15:10.800 --> 15:11.840
Nothing has happened.

15:11.920 --> 15:13.040
Nor will it.

15:13.120 --> 15:15.240
He would die without his eyes.

15:16.880 --> 15:18.840
And out of kindness,
Tommy would offer his daughter

15:18.920 --> 15:21.720
a place in one of his institutions
for orphaned girls.

15:22.240 --> 15:24.080
Or even take her into the family.

15:25.280 --> 15:26.840
And it would begin again.

15:31.880 --> 15:33.520
What is the thing, Linda?

15:34.680 --> 15:36.360
The thing you can't put aside?

15:39.960 --> 15:41.440
It's not Arthur.

15:43.040 --> 15:45.040
It's who I am when he's there.

15:46.840 --> 15:50.600
God hears every filthy word in my head,
knows every dirty thing.

15:51.360 --> 15:53.480
And your Friends don't use filthy words?

15:53.560 --> 15:56.040
If I fall this time,
I'll fall all the way.

15:57.040 --> 16:00.160
Perhaps it's what you deserve
with your filthy words.

16:01.800 --> 16:02.640
[Lizzie chuckles]

16:04.480 --> 16:05.600
I used to fuck seven men a day,

16:05.680 --> 16:07.720
and now I'm learning
how to ride a horse side-saddle.

16:12.400 --> 16:14.280
There's good and there's evil.

16:15.560 --> 16:16.760
There's both mixed.

16:18.560 --> 16:20.800
And that's Arthur and you and me.

16:21.360 --> 16:24.120
You don't get what you deserve,
you get what you take.

16:26.240 --> 16:27.440
What about him?

16:32.440 --> 16:34.640
[Lizzie] He's making up his mind.

16:36.880 --> 16:37.880
[footsteps approaching]

16:41.520 --> 16:42.360
[door opens]

16:46.760 --> 16:49.520
Someone called Polly Gray to see you.

16:52.320 --> 16:54.000
Yes or no?

16:54.840 --> 16:55.840
Yes.

16:56.560 --> 16:57.440
[footsteps receding]

17:01.480 --> 17:02.480
[footsteps approaching]

17:18.160 --> 17:20.000
[Ada] I've come to take you to the clinic.

17:20.079 --> 17:22.400
I already told Michael.
My husband or no one.

17:22.480 --> 17:23.560
I've got a car.

17:24.240 --> 17:27.119
They have taxis.
Even in this fucking city.

17:27.200 --> 17:29.359
Look, if they don't hear a heartbeat,

17:29.440 --> 17:32.160
they're gonna give you options.
None of them are nice.

17:33.520 --> 17:35.560
I had my check-up three days ago.

17:35.640 --> 17:37.160
They heard a beating heart.

17:37.240 --> 17:40.560
But if they had told me
that baby had died inside of me,

17:40.640 --> 17:42.280
I would have wanted someone with me.

17:44.320 --> 17:46.840
My husband may do as he's told, but, er...

17:47.600 --> 17:48.600
I don't.

17:48.680 --> 17:51.720
Look, if they hear a heartbeat,
you won't need anybody with you,

17:51.800 --> 17:55.040
'cause you'll have the baby with you.
So I will leave you alone.

17:55.120 --> 17:58.680
But if you get in a taxi in this city
and they hear your accent,

17:58.760 --> 18:01.120
they'll take you on a grand tour.

18:03.840 --> 18:05.000
Come on.

18:10.480 --> 18:11.920
[Karl] So, when will Mum be home?

18:12.560 --> 18:14.200
[Younger] She said
she had to go to Birmingham.

18:14.280 --> 18:15.360
Do you want me to cook you something?

18:15.440 --> 18:16.480
Cook?

18:17.200 --> 18:18.200
You're a man.

18:23.000 --> 18:25.680
[Younger] This is really not fair.

18:25.760 --> 18:27.720
Your mother never told me
you were this good.

18:28.240 --> 18:30.520
I'm in a club. I'm champion.

18:31.080 --> 18:33.120
I've beat people even older than you.

18:33.200 --> 18:34.720
Even older than me?

18:34.800 --> 18:35.640
[scoffs]

18:37.960 --> 18:41.680
At school, some of the children say
that black people and Jews are worse.

18:42.760 --> 18:43.600
Worse than what?

18:45.160 --> 18:46.320
Than anything.

18:47.560 --> 18:49.760
And one teacher, Mr Hudson,

18:49.840 --> 18:51.880
he calls my friend "the little Jew boy."

18:53.640 --> 18:55.440
[breathes deeply]

18:56.200 --> 18:57.120
Karl,

18:57.600 --> 19:00.760
these days,
there are some very stupid people

19:00.840 --> 19:02.800
saying some very stupid things.

19:03.480 --> 19:04.320
Okay?

19:06.560 --> 19:07.600
What do you think?

19:13.880 --> 19:14.880
Checkmate.

19:18.120 --> 19:19.880
I think I don't want you to be my dad...

19:21.360 --> 19:24.160
'cause my dad's white and he's in heaven.

19:28.880 --> 19:29.840
[footsteps receding]

19:44.800 --> 19:48.360
[Polly] I came to see you in hospital
to tell you there is a strategy in place.

19:48.840 --> 19:50.400
Not to break you out.

19:50.480 --> 19:51.480
[Aberama] Don't worry.

19:51.560 --> 19:53.240
My sister will look after me.

19:57.560 --> 19:59.040
You must stay here,

19:59.880 --> 20:02.520
and you'll let Tommy deal with the men
who killed your son.

20:11.920 --> 20:13.720
You're 45 today?

20:16.360 --> 20:18.520
I'm probably a bit older than that.

20:19.600 --> 20:20.840
Probably.

20:23.360 --> 20:25.000
I've dealt death.

20:26.600 --> 20:28.600
Now death has dealt with me.

20:30.560 --> 20:32.360
I have one more killing to do,

20:33.120 --> 20:34.640
then I'll be done.

20:39.000 --> 20:40.920
Happy birthday, Polly Gray.

20:52.880 --> 20:54.000
[Aberama and woman greeting in Romani]

21:00.280 --> 21:01.120
[Aberama grunts]

21:23.240 --> 21:24.080
[engine starts]

21:38.560 --> 21:40.080
Get a car and a driver.

21:40.160 --> 21:42.320
Find out where the Fury family are camped.

21:43.160 --> 21:44.640
I need their men to help me.

21:45.400 --> 21:48.720
I need my hunting rifle, 50 bullets.

21:49.680 --> 21:51.240
I'm going to Scotland...

21:51.720 --> 21:52.640
tonight.

22:04.440 --> 22:05.280
[door unlocks]

22:10.120 --> 22:11.480
[Younger] I was expecting Ada.

22:11.560 --> 22:13.640
Yeah. Give you a key, did she?

22:13.720 --> 22:16.080
I was meant to meet her today,
but she said she had to go to Birmingham.

22:16.160 --> 22:19.120
Yes, Tommy sent her on a mission.
She's doing my job for me.

22:19.200 --> 22:20.920
Where's Karl, eh? Where's the boy?

22:21.000 --> 22:22.480
He went to buy an ice cream.

22:22.560 --> 22:24.440
Ada said to tell you she'd be late.

22:24.520 --> 22:25.560
[Younger] You knew I'd be here?

22:25.640 --> 22:27.320
Yeah. We knew you'd be here.

22:27.400 --> 22:29.040
We have some business for you.

22:36.920 --> 22:37.760
[Michael snorting]

22:39.520 --> 22:40.360
[exhales]

22:41.200 --> 22:44.680
Any business I have with you, Mr Shelby,
is meant to be strictly confidential.

22:45.240 --> 22:47.360
Er, Michael, you still have
shit on your shoes.

22:47.440 --> 22:49.400
My associate here can evidently smell it.

22:49.480 --> 22:50.720
I don't mean any offence.

22:50.800 --> 22:54.840
Here, Michael. Go and find Karl
and buy him an ice cream, eh?

22:55.360 --> 22:56.960
The man doesn't trust you.

22:58.800 --> 22:59.680
Fuck you, Tom.

23:07.640 --> 23:09.120
You know, Gina phoned.

23:13.160 --> 23:14.920
Baby's heart's beating strong.

23:15.960 --> 23:17.800
But I swear to God, Tom,

23:17.880 --> 23:20.800
by the time that baby
draws his first breath,

23:20.880 --> 23:22.560
-you and I will be done.
-[Tommy scoffs]

23:26.760 --> 23:28.400
And you will be king.

23:28.880 --> 23:29.880
Is that it, Michael?

23:33.120 --> 23:34.280
You know, Tom,

23:34.920 --> 23:36.600
there are doctors in London now

23:36.680 --> 23:38.600
who can talk their way into your head.

23:38.680 --> 23:40.120
Dig out all the shit.

23:40.960 --> 23:42.560
Perhaps you should see one.

23:44.920 --> 23:45.760
[coughs]

23:52.680 --> 23:53.960
You're still not alone.

23:56.600 --> 23:59.400
Me brother and I are the same person.

23:59.480 --> 24:00.600
Here.

24:00.680 --> 24:02.080
There's a letter from Mosley.

24:02.640 --> 24:03.840
You should read it.

24:18.040 --> 24:20.000
What investigation is he talking about?

24:22.160 --> 24:25.840
Two weeks ago,
a journalist was killed in Maida Vale.

24:25.920 --> 24:26.880
The night before,

24:26.960 --> 24:30.320
he'd come to me about some story
he was going to write about me.

24:31.120 --> 24:32.760
We had nothing to do with that killing.

24:33.440 --> 24:35.000
[Younger] Mosley wants you as his deputy?

24:36.720 --> 24:39.320
His constituency is Smethwick.
It borders me own.

24:39.400 --> 24:41.000
And he wants Birmingham as his stronghold.

24:41.080 --> 24:44.480
He knows I have strong support
among working people.

24:45.120 --> 24:46.840
We help him out with rallies,

24:47.360 --> 24:49.440
and show up at some town hall meetings.

24:49.520 --> 24:51.960
Right, and why are you
showing this letter to me?

24:52.920 --> 24:54.200
A Minister of State...

24:54.920 --> 24:56.920
who may have seditious intentions.

24:57.000 --> 24:59.000
There's no proof of sedition
in this letter.

24:59.080 --> 25:00.720
[Tommy] You work in intelligence, Younger.

25:00.800 --> 25:03.240
You don't need proof.
Give it to your superiors.

25:03.320 --> 25:06.680
Mr Shelby, I have a very specific brief.

25:06.760 --> 25:10.560
My brief is specifically
to gather information

25:10.640 --> 25:12.640
on the activities of communists.

25:15.160 --> 25:18.640
Your immediate superior
in the intelligence unit

25:18.720 --> 25:20.720
is a Colonel Patrick Wyatt, yeah?

25:21.800 --> 25:26.200
I understand he regularly plays polo
with Oswald Mosley.

25:27.040 --> 25:29.920
They share membership of various clubs
in London and Birmingham.

25:30.600 --> 25:31.880
[Younger] I have specific orders.

25:31.960 --> 25:33.920
I am a soldier. I--

25:34.000 --> 25:35.560
You think you can join this family?

25:38.200 --> 25:40.400
I have no intention of joining a family.

25:41.440 --> 25:44.640
Oh, thank fuck for that,
'cause, er, you'd hate our weddings.

25:44.720 --> 25:46.240
I thought you said
this was about business.

25:46.320 --> 25:48.840
Yes. Family business
and government business.

25:48.920 --> 25:50.200
All in one envelope.

25:54.920 --> 25:56.000
Younger...

25:56.840 --> 25:58.760
listen to me. Forget about Ada.

25:59.280 --> 26:00.600
Forget about weddings.

26:01.920 --> 26:04.040
You know what Mosley represents.

26:05.680 --> 26:07.080
You know his philosophy.

26:09.120 --> 26:12.640
Now, I'm planning to reply to him
and tell him that I'm making up me mind.

26:14.640 --> 26:16.960
But in the meantime,
you need to give me instruction.

26:17.040 --> 26:18.680
I could fight him on me own if I have to,

26:19.320 --> 26:22.000
or I could join his organisation

26:22.920 --> 26:25.360
and undermine him on behalf of the King.

26:27.240 --> 26:29.080
But you need to make a decision.

26:31.760 --> 26:32.600
[exhales heavily]

26:42.480 --> 26:43.320
[sighs]

26:44.640 --> 26:45.480
[smacks lips]

26:46.160 --> 26:49.680
I suppose there are a few things
I can do on my own initiative.

27:01.600 --> 27:02.560
[door opens]

27:02.640 --> 27:03.520
[exhales]

27:03.600 --> 27:04.480
[objects clatter]

27:15.280 --> 27:16.560
On your fucking feet.

27:18.600 --> 27:19.480
[breathing heavily]

27:20.120 --> 27:21.280
Hello, Tom.

27:23.200 --> 27:25.320
I thought you were staying over in London.

27:26.320 --> 27:27.400
Hello, Johnny.

27:28.640 --> 27:29.960
How are you, eh?

27:30.440 --> 27:31.280
[door closes]

27:31.840 --> 27:33.080
How are your ribs?

27:34.160 --> 27:35.120
Are you managing?

27:35.680 --> 27:37.480
-Just about, Tom, yeah.
-Yeah? Good.

27:38.520 --> 27:39.360
And who's that?

27:41.960 --> 27:44.880
Is it Maisy or is it Clara?

27:45.960 --> 27:46.800
Ah.

27:47.760 --> 27:48.640
Sandra.

27:49.280 --> 27:50.480
Well, may I say,

27:51.520 --> 27:52.640
your breakfasts...

27:53.400 --> 27:54.720
are a great improvement.

27:55.720 --> 27:56.920
[shakily] Mr Shelby,

27:57.600 --> 27:58.520
I'm sorry.

27:59.200 --> 28:00.560
Don't worry, Sandra.

28:01.480 --> 28:05.480
The only way to get fired
from this household is through burnt toast

28:06.440 --> 28:08.040
or talking to the police.

28:08.120 --> 28:09.360
Go on, go to bed.

28:11.240 --> 28:12.240
And, Sandra...

28:13.720 --> 28:16.160
everything Johnny said is lies.

28:19.400 --> 28:21.080
-[scoffs]
-[door opens]

28:21.160 --> 28:23.480
-Johnny, Johnny, Johnny.
-[door closes]

28:23.560 --> 28:25.600
While you was gone, I got a message, Tom.

28:26.480 --> 28:28.480
A cousin of Aberama Gold.

28:28.560 --> 28:30.080
Galloped from Meriden.

28:30.760 --> 28:32.280
He said Aberama wants you to know

28:32.360 --> 28:35.520
that he's gone to Scotland
to deal with his business himself,

28:35.600 --> 28:37.160
and that you'd know what that meant.

28:39.440 --> 28:40.520
Fuck!

28:41.240 --> 28:45.240
The boy said Aberama arrived
from the hospital in Polly's Bentley.

28:47.120 --> 28:49.000
She fucking helped him?

28:49.080 --> 28:49.920
[chuckles]

28:51.440 --> 28:53.360
She fucking helped him.

28:54.520 --> 28:57.040
But it can't be love, 'cause it's Polly.

28:58.080 --> 28:59.880
'Cause it's fucking Polly.

29:01.400 --> 29:03.400
[sighs] All right, Johnny,
I have a job for you.

29:03.480 --> 29:04.720
Tom, I'm in a lot of pain here.

29:05.320 --> 29:07.720
I need you to go and find Aberama Gold.

29:07.800 --> 29:10.400
He has kin on the Lothian border.
The Fury family.

29:10.480 --> 29:11.960
For fuck's sake, Tom!

29:12.040 --> 29:15.520
The Furys,
they don't even use words to fucking talk.

29:15.600 --> 29:17.160
Just hand gestures and fucking howls.

29:17.240 --> 29:19.280
You will go to them and you will find him.

29:19.360 --> 29:22.640
-Tom, I am in fucking pain here.
-Yeah, you appear to be managing.

29:22.720 --> 29:24.000
I said I was just managing.

29:24.080 --> 29:26.840
Well, you can just manage
to sit in a car with Arthur

29:26.920 --> 29:29.120
and follow the patrin
to find the Fury family.

29:29.200 --> 29:32.480
Arthur will take care of everything
that requires bones and muscles.

29:32.560 --> 29:33.920
I warned you, Tom.

29:34.000 --> 29:35.400
The Golds will be the death of one of us.

29:35.960 --> 29:36.880
[door closes]

29:36.960 --> 29:40.080
And it looks like
it's going to be fucking me! Ow!

29:41.600 --> 29:42.680
Well, go on.

29:43.560 --> 29:44.560
Open it.

29:48.880 --> 29:49.880
[Polly] So...

29:51.800 --> 29:53.480
you heard the baby's heartbeat today.

29:53.560 --> 29:54.400
[chuckles]

29:55.320 --> 29:56.480
Beats so fast.

29:57.840 --> 29:59.760
Would have been a birthday gift enough.

30:01.120 --> 30:02.240
New life.

30:07.000 --> 30:07.840
[Gina] Liberty.

30:10.160 --> 30:11.160
Freedom.

30:17.640 --> 30:18.960
Feels like a weapon.

30:19.880 --> 30:22.280
I only came because
Michael's driving back from London,

30:22.360 --> 30:24.480
and he said he didn't want you
to be on your own.

30:28.520 --> 30:29.360
So...

30:31.080 --> 30:33.000
whose idea was the gift of freedom?

30:34.400 --> 30:35.240
Mine.

30:37.480 --> 30:40.120
You want to take Michael
and the baby to New York?

30:40.920 --> 30:41.920
Yes.

30:42.800 --> 30:45.680
The baby will have two grandmothers.
The other one lives--

30:45.760 --> 30:48.280
The other one lives amongst human beings.

30:48.960 --> 30:51.120
The other one is a human being.

30:52.000 --> 30:53.960
-[Gina sighs]
-It's all right,

30:54.600 --> 30:55.720
I'm not drunk.

30:56.560 --> 30:57.640
I'm just free.

30:58.880 --> 31:00.240
So, what do you want?

31:02.120 --> 31:03.480
My approval?

31:06.880 --> 31:07.880
Your help.

31:08.880 --> 31:11.520
Michael wants you to come with us.

31:12.760 --> 31:15.480
We can all live in Long Island,
right on the beach.

31:17.200 --> 31:19.000
Isn't Long Island in Australia?

31:21.080 --> 31:23.480
Or is it in California
amongst the Indians?

31:23.560 --> 31:24.640
It's in New York,

31:25.160 --> 31:26.000
Polly.

31:27.960 --> 31:30.120
You see, we all try and get away.

31:32.920 --> 31:34.120
But we never do.

31:45.720 --> 31:48.320
I wish I felt that heartbeat today.

31:53.240 --> 31:56.040
You're starting to sound
a little sorry for yourself.

31:59.720 --> 32:01.080
I'm an American.

32:02.360 --> 32:06.160
We don't just go round and round
and round. We go in a straight line.

32:07.200 --> 32:08.800
And my baby...

32:09.680 --> 32:11.520
will be born in New York.

32:19.800 --> 32:20.640
[door opens]

32:22.200 --> 32:23.040
[door closes]

32:23.560 --> 32:26.680
I'm not happy about moving this meeting
to licensed premises.

32:28.440 --> 32:30.760
You've saved your union the train fare,

32:31.560 --> 32:33.280
and you hate London anyway.

32:33.360 --> 32:36.600
We are looking for popular speakers
for our upcoming rally.

32:36.680 --> 32:39.160
You're making quite a name for yourself
in the Commons.

32:39.840 --> 32:40.920
Betty!

32:42.080 --> 32:44.360
-What are you drinking?
-Water.

32:45.760 --> 32:47.360
Bottle of champagne, Betty.

32:47.440 --> 32:48.520
You'll drink it on your own.

32:48.600 --> 32:49.800
[Tommy] That's the idea.

32:49.880 --> 32:51.960
Shall we sit down, Miss Eden?

33:02.280 --> 33:03.120
[grunts]

33:17.800 --> 33:18.800
Revolution.

33:21.160 --> 33:24.120
So, how is life as a socialist?

33:26.680 --> 33:27.880
This glass...

33:29.000 --> 33:29.880
The bubbles...

33:32.120 --> 33:33.600
They rise to the top.

33:35.320 --> 33:37.600
Each bubble has the same chance to rise.

33:38.400 --> 33:40.640
That's a very peculiar form of socialism.

33:41.240 --> 33:42.640
And this bottle...

33:44.760 --> 33:46.520
Once the cork comes out,

33:48.240 --> 33:49.800
you can't get it back in.

33:50.520 --> 33:52.400
You need to finish what you started.

33:54.320 --> 33:56.320
It's cleverness, that's all.

33:59.600 --> 34:01.080
So, you're playing at this?

34:01.840 --> 34:03.880
Yeah, people can be turned around.

34:05.360 --> 34:07.400
-Even your people.
-My people?

34:07.480 --> 34:08.320
Yeah.

34:08.960 --> 34:10.400
For them, it's just the same.

34:11.400 --> 34:13.000
Communism, fascism.

34:14.159 --> 34:16.920
For most people,
it's an apple and an apple.

34:17.000 --> 34:19.040
Fascism is the subject of the rally.

34:19.120 --> 34:21.199
I want you to speak against it.

34:22.120 --> 34:23.679
In answer to your question,

34:25.159 --> 34:27.120
I cannot address your rally...

34:28.560 --> 34:31.040
because it's not part of
the current strategy.

34:34.080 --> 34:35.400
Are you okay, Thomas?

34:36.960 --> 34:39.040
Do you want a man to carry you home?

34:39.520 --> 34:41.199
[glass tumbles]

34:41.280 --> 34:44.000
I knew we should not have had this meeting
on licensed premises.

34:49.600 --> 34:50.440
[door opens]

34:51.440 --> 34:52.280
[door closes]

34:59.120 --> 35:00.880
[Grace] Happy or sad, Thomas?

35:12.760 --> 35:13.920
I warn you...

35:14.800 --> 35:16.040
I'll break your heart.

35:26.360 --> 35:27.200
[Tommy coughs]

35:31.120 --> 35:32.760
I didn't expect you home.

35:36.960 --> 35:39.040
Frances said Linda was here today.

35:39.760 --> 35:42.800
Frances has a very specific loyalty,
doesn't she?

35:44.240 --> 35:45.080
Well,

35:45.760 --> 35:48.200
people are loyal
to those who pay their wages.

35:49.880 --> 35:53.680
Also, Maggie at the exchange
said you made some calls.

35:54.360 --> 35:56.280
Then you'll know I called a solicitor.

35:57.080 --> 35:59.400
Did Maggie listen in to the conversation?

36:05.240 --> 36:07.160
He said he'd represent me.

36:08.360 --> 36:09.960
But I put the phone down.

36:11.520 --> 36:13.400
There and then, I made a decision.

36:15.440 --> 36:17.400
And when I heard your car pull up,

36:18.520 --> 36:19.960
I got changed.

36:24.760 --> 36:27.480
You said in your head,
you still pay for it.

36:28.880 --> 36:31.120
So I have decided to continue
to take the payment

36:31.200 --> 36:34.760
and balance my heart against my head
as though it were a book of accounts.

36:35.480 --> 36:37.440
Value my head a shilling more.

36:37.520 --> 36:38.360
[Tommy chuckles]

36:42.640 --> 36:46.520
When was the last time
you had to worry about shillings?

36:46.600 --> 36:47.480
Eh?

36:48.880 --> 36:51.440
People are loyal to those
who pay their wages.

36:52.840 --> 36:54.680
So I will be loyal to you.

36:56.760 --> 36:58.680
But this is the deal.

36:59.480 --> 37:01.960
You don't fuck anybody else in my house.

37:02.600 --> 37:06.680
Nor within a day of holding our child
by the hand. A day on either side.

37:08.760 --> 37:12.960
And you let me in sometimes.
Into your head.

37:16.720 --> 37:18.440
To clear it out.

37:18.520 --> 37:20.560
That what needs clearing out.

37:21.680 --> 37:22.520
Agreed.

37:28.080 --> 37:29.160
And this...

37:30.680 --> 37:31.720
always.

37:33.920 --> 37:35.200
[Tommy] The deal is,

37:35.920 --> 37:37.360
you belong to me.

37:38.720 --> 37:39.960
My property.

37:41.360 --> 37:43.200
No one touches my property.

37:46.880 --> 37:49.840
I touch myself, but it's still you anyway,

37:49.920 --> 37:52.120
so that's why I put the phone down.

37:58.520 --> 37:59.520
No, Tom.

38:00.080 --> 38:01.760
We do it in the bed at least.

38:05.280 --> 38:07.040
[both breathing heavily and moaning]

38:16.360 --> 38:17.200
[chuckles]

38:17.280 --> 38:19.720
[whispers] Everything is mine, Lizzie.

38:21.840 --> 38:22.960
Everything.

38:28.360 --> 38:29.600
[Lizzie moaning]

38:40.840 --> 38:42.000
[phone ringing]

38:47.720 --> 38:48.560
[grunts]

38:51.880 --> 38:52.720
[line rings]

38:53.840 --> 38:54.720
[line connects]

38:54.800 --> 38:55.800
[Tommy] Arthur?

38:56.400 --> 38:58.240
-Yeah?
-Frances was right.

38:59.040 --> 39:00.160
Linda was here today.

39:00.240 --> 39:01.840
[grunts] Fuck.

39:02.360 --> 39:03.680
What did she say, huh?

39:05.280 --> 39:06.920
I just want to talk to her, that's all.

39:07.000 --> 39:09.960
Arthur, listen. First I need you
to go to Scotland

39:10.040 --> 39:13.360
and bring back Aberama Gold.
Then we'll go and we'll find Linda.

39:13.440 --> 39:15.920
No, no, no.

39:16.000 --> 39:17.280
I'll keep calling you, Tom.

39:19.880 --> 39:21.160
You know I will.

39:22.480 --> 39:24.320
I'll call this number back.

39:25.360 --> 39:28.360
Again, again, and again.

39:29.240 --> 39:30.480
If you do not answer,

39:31.200 --> 39:32.600
I'll jump in my fucking car

39:32.680 --> 39:35.160
and I'll drive to your house.
You know I will.

39:37.560 --> 39:38.760
I'll stay there all night if I have to.

39:38.840 --> 39:40.800
I won't go nowhere.

39:40.880 --> 39:44.960
Not Scotland, until you tell me
what it is you know.

39:45.040 --> 39:45.880
[sighs]

39:55.920 --> 39:57.200
[Tommy] All right, listen to me.

39:57.280 --> 39:58.960
I don't have an address.

40:00.280 --> 40:02.600
But she's with the Quakers in Bournville.

40:04.040 --> 40:07.000
Apparently, there is someone
who is a Friend.

40:08.400 --> 40:10.160
He had a wife who died...

40:11.360 --> 40:14.480
from Spanish flu in 1918.
He has a daughter.

40:15.080 --> 40:16.280
That should be enough to find him. 

40:16.760 --> 40:17.600
And Arthur,

40:18.200 --> 40:21.400
just talk to him
and get a message to Linda.

40:22.520 --> 40:24.520
Nothing happened, Arthur.

40:25.720 --> 40:29.880
He's a Quaker who is a friend.
They're not like us, they talk.

40:29.960 --> 40:32.240
Oh, I'll speak to him. Hmm.

40:32.920 --> 40:34.280
Man to man.

40:35.280 --> 40:36.960
And then after that,

40:37.880 --> 40:39.440
I'll go up north, hmm.

40:40.040 --> 40:42.760
Deal with our business. I promise ya.

40:43.320 --> 40:45.520
Arthur. Arthur, listen to me...

41:00.080 --> 41:00.920
[door closes]

41:01.720 --> 41:03.000
[Lizzie] Who were you talking to?

41:03.880 --> 41:07.440
I have to ask you 'cause Maggie
at the exchange won't tell me.

41:07.520 --> 41:08.600
Who was it?

41:09.400 --> 41:10.720
Was it Arthur?

41:10.800 --> 41:11.640
[inhales sharply]

41:12.760 --> 41:14.480
I need me brother in one piece.

41:15.160 --> 41:17.160
Arthur makes his own decisions.

41:19.040 --> 41:20.640
You marry a Shelby,

41:21.560 --> 41:23.560
you stay fucking married.

41:25.160 --> 41:26.200
-[door opens]
-[Lizzie] Fuck.

41:28.160 --> 41:29.040
[door closes]

41:32.560 --> 41:34.280
Well, look at this, hmm?

41:34.360 --> 41:35.200
Can I help you?

41:35.880 --> 41:37.240
Yeah, I think you can.

41:38.040 --> 41:41.160
I'm looking for Linda Shelby.

41:41.240 --> 41:42.280
Do you know her?

41:44.120 --> 41:44.960
Eh?

41:45.040 --> 41:46.320
I'm Arthur...

41:47.400 --> 41:48.520
her husband.

41:49.880 --> 41:52.640
If you're her husband,
she doesn't want to talk to you.

41:53.680 --> 41:55.280
Well, look at you.

41:55.360 --> 41:56.200
[chuckles]

41:57.320 --> 41:59.040
Ain't you smart?

41:59.120 --> 41:59.960
Eh?

42:00.560 --> 42:03.480
What, you got all the fucking answers,
have ya?

42:03.560 --> 42:05.600
Well, let's try you with another one, huh?

42:06.560 --> 42:08.800
Let's try you with another one.
How about...

42:08.880 --> 42:13.680
How about we search
for the fucking truth within, hmm?

42:13.760 --> 42:16.000
Let's have a look, all right?
Let's have a look.

42:16.080 --> 42:17.840
Let's see what we've got inside here, eh?

42:17.920 --> 42:19.960
-Inside, you fucking bastard!
-[groaning]

42:26.000 --> 42:26.960
[Arthur] Hey...

42:27.480 --> 42:28.640
you wanna keep looking, eh?

42:29.520 --> 42:32.600
♪ She'll go ♪

42:34.920 --> 42:38.480
♪ She'll lay belief on you ♪

42:38.560 --> 42:39.440
[man whimpering]

42:42.440 --> 42:43.560
[grunting and groaning]

42:46.040 --> 42:50.200
♪ How can life become her point of view ♪

42:53.200 --> 42:58.760
♪ And when the clothes are strewn ♪

43:00.160 --> 43:05.480
♪ Don't be afraid of the room ♪

43:05.560 --> 43:08.560
♪ Touch the fullness of her breast ♪

43:08.640 --> 43:14.040
♪ Feel the love of her caress... ♪

43:14.120 --> 43:15.840
-[Arthur] Hey...
-[groaning]

43:15.920 --> 43:17.360
I will ask you again.

43:18.320 --> 43:20.080
Eh? Eh?

43:20.720 --> 43:23.840
I'll ask you again. Come here,
listen, listen. Get up.

43:25.040 --> 43:26.720
Where is she?

43:26.800 --> 43:27.640
Eh?

43:28.440 --> 43:29.440
Where is she?

43:32.720 --> 43:33.800
[man] No.

43:33.880 --> 43:34.720
[Arthur] Eh.

43:34.800 --> 43:36.160
[man] No. No, no, no!

43:36.240 --> 43:42.440
♪ She will be your living end ♪

43:46.040 --> 43:46.920
[knife slashes]

43:51.000 --> 43:52.040
[indistinct shouting]

43:55.160 --> 43:56.080
[Arthur breathing heavily]

44:01.840 --> 44:02.680
[chuckles]

44:06.720 --> 44:08.200
I'm a good man.

44:09.680 --> 44:12.960
I'm a fucking good man like you.

44:13.040 --> 44:13.920
[sobbing]

44:17.360 --> 44:19.160
A God-fearing man.

44:20.680 --> 44:22.720
And there's good in my heart.

44:23.680 --> 44:26.040
There is good in my heart!

44:32.600 --> 44:33.840
But my hands...

44:34.880 --> 44:37.280
These hands belong to the devil.

44:39.080 --> 44:41.200
The fucking devil!

44:44.080 --> 44:45.560
[crying and sniffling]

44:50.160 --> 44:52.840
Right. I...

45:14.000 --> 45:15.160
[Strong] Did she come back?

45:16.760 --> 45:17.760
No.

45:20.520 --> 45:22.480
[Strong] Is she in Scotland?
Is that why you're going?

45:22.560 --> 45:25.080
No, she's not
in fucking Scotland, Charlie.

45:27.640 --> 45:30.400
Whiskey. We want whiskey.

45:30.480 --> 45:32.760
Maps. Cigars.

45:32.840 --> 45:34.560
Load the van. We want it all.

45:34.640 --> 45:35.480
Who's "we"?

45:35.560 --> 45:37.120
Me and Johnny Dogs.

45:37.200 --> 45:38.040
Ah.

45:39.440 --> 45:41.840
So it's you and Johnny Dogs
against Scotland.

45:45.040 --> 45:46.120
You know, at the BSA,

45:46.200 --> 45:48.600
our friends could get you
some of them new artillery cannons

45:48.680 --> 45:50.840
that fire ten shells a second.

45:50.920 --> 45:53.440
You can mount one
on the roof of your fucking car.

45:54.240 --> 45:55.520
Petrol.

45:55.600 --> 45:57.120
Need petrol.

45:57.200 --> 46:00.360
It's so far up north,
they run out of the bloody stuff.

46:01.400 --> 46:02.240
Yeah.

46:02.720 --> 46:05.600
Still riding around on fucking chariots,
they are.

46:09.080 --> 46:12.200
Curly, Arthur is going to Scotland,
so he needs hand grenades.

46:12.800 --> 46:13.640
[Curly] How many?

46:13.720 --> 46:15.720
Fuck's sake, it's like it's normal.

46:16.400 --> 46:18.880
[hesitantly] Our friends at the BSA
still have lots left from the war,

46:18.960 --> 46:21.000
but we can't give them away, yeah?

46:21.080 --> 46:22.920
Get me some hand grenades, Curly, eh?

46:23.000 --> 46:23.920
-Hmm?
-[chuckles nervously]

46:24.000 --> 46:26.480
You find them back there, eh?
Good boy, yeah?

46:26.560 --> 46:28.000
Go get me some.

46:28.080 --> 46:29.760
-Put them on my account.
-Yeah.

46:33.040 --> 46:34.320
[whispers] How many?

46:34.400 --> 46:35.280
Three, Curly.

46:35.360 --> 46:37.400
Three, three. Right, yeah.

46:42.880 --> 46:45.120
Find a way of getting her back, Arthur.

46:48.000 --> 46:50.360
Without her,
you're as good as dead already.

47:15.520 --> 47:17.680
That's them. The Billy Boys.

47:38.720 --> 47:39.600
Gentlemen,

47:40.600 --> 47:45.480
you have just crossed the border
into the County of East Tollcross.

47:46.320 --> 47:49.760
Now, according to
the unwritten constitution

47:49.840 --> 47:51.520
of Tollcross County,

47:52.120 --> 47:54.680
Gypsies, Catholics,

47:54.760 --> 47:57.160
and other criminally-minded individuals

47:57.240 --> 48:00.640
are not allowed to work the roads
of our Protestant district,

48:00.720 --> 48:03.600
on account of the poor quality
of their labour.

48:03.680 --> 48:07.000
So, my own boys
will be taking over from here.

48:07.640 --> 48:12.200
We will be needing your tools,
your tar, your burner,

48:13.400 --> 48:15.520
and your transportation.

48:16.680 --> 48:19.760
You're Gypsies.
You can easily steal another.

48:21.520 --> 48:24.080
I have the keys to the truck.

48:42.720 --> 48:43.560
[keys jingling]

48:50.720 --> 48:52.000
[groans]

48:52.560 --> 48:53.960
[men grunting and groaning]

49:09.120 --> 49:11.000
-[bones cracking]
-[screaming]

49:16.560 --> 49:17.480
Now...

49:19.120 --> 49:23.080
I want you boys to take a message
back to Jimmy McCavern.

49:23.160 --> 49:24.960
"You killed my son.

49:25.040 --> 49:27.000
-You hoisted him on a cross!"
-[groans]

49:30.680 --> 49:31.800
In this gun...

49:33.640 --> 49:34.880
there is a bullet.

49:35.600 --> 49:38.800
And on it is carved the name McCavern.

49:43.120 --> 49:45.920
And when the time comes
for his crucifixion,

49:46.640 --> 49:50.960
it will be me who drives in the nails!

50:09.000 --> 50:10.200
[screaming]

50:34.160 --> 50:35.640
Mr Shelby!

50:36.600 --> 50:38.080
At last you are alone.

50:40.400 --> 50:42.560
I think we'll make quite the team.

50:44.280 --> 50:46.440
The pheasants won't know what hit them.

50:46.520 --> 50:47.600
-[wings flapping]
-[gunshots]

50:51.360 --> 50:53.440
You're a fine shot, Mr Shelby.

50:55.200 --> 50:56.760
You were in the yeomanry, yes?

50:57.560 --> 50:58.840
You were cavalry.

50:59.440 --> 51:01.720
You won the Distinguished Service medal.

51:02.360 --> 51:03.480
That will help.

51:04.920 --> 51:05.960
With what?

51:07.240 --> 51:09.440
Two months ago, I was in Rome.

51:09.520 --> 51:11.040
I met Mr Mussolini.

51:11.960 --> 51:14.200
You and I, and men like him...

51:14.280 --> 51:15.200
[wings flapping]

51:16.000 --> 51:17.640
...we will shape the future.

51:20.360 --> 51:22.480
When will you resign
from the Labour party?

51:25.200 --> 51:28.080
The day before I announce
the formation of my new party.

51:30.720 --> 51:35.800
The British Union of Fascists will be born
on January the 1st of next year.

51:36.920 --> 51:38.680
First day of a new decade.

51:40.720 --> 51:44.600
The 1930s, Mr Shelby, will belong to us.

51:47.320 --> 51:48.680
Did you bring that cigar?

51:51.840 --> 51:53.320
Before we smoke,

51:54.320 --> 51:55.640
I have some conditions.

51:58.080 --> 52:00.800
It really isn't going to be
that kind of relationship.

52:04.600 --> 52:07.200
Just smoke like the fine man
you will become.

52:15.520 --> 52:16.520
[bell tolling]

52:22.680 --> 52:24.880
Yes, Colonel Ben Younger.

52:24.960 --> 52:27.880
I have an allocated confidential line.
Code 78.

52:28.840 --> 52:30.480
[breathes deeply]

52:30.560 --> 52:32.120
It's me. [clears throat]

52:32.680 --> 52:34.480
I've agreed to work with our friend.

52:35.320 --> 52:37.360
He is going to announce on January 1st.

52:38.240 --> 52:39.560
I need to know that my position

52:39.640 --> 52:42.440
as informant against him
is officially sanctioned.

52:46.400 --> 52:48.160
[band playing]

52:50.480 --> 52:52.440
Today, gentlemen,

52:53.080 --> 52:58.560
we are avenging an unprovoked attack
on members of our organisation

52:58.640 --> 53:02.120
who were simply carrying out
a routine border patrol.

53:03.240 --> 53:05.640
Our enemies are Gypsies,

53:05.720 --> 53:09.920
members of a race
destined for natural eradication anyway,

53:10.000 --> 53:13.480
due to what the scientists call selection.

53:14.720 --> 53:18.760
And since these beggars are unchristened
and unregistered,

53:18.840 --> 53:23.320
the local constabulary will as soon
drop them in a communal grave

53:23.400 --> 53:25.640
as find a name for a gravestone.

53:27.080 --> 53:29.840
So, proceed in any manner you choose

53:29.920 --> 53:31.920
to find the fugitive we seek.

53:36.440 --> 53:37.440
[band playing in distance]

53:38.240 --> 53:39.080
[gun cocks]

53:39.160 --> 53:40.000
[gasps]

53:40.800 --> 53:42.200
Morning, Mr Gold.

53:43.200 --> 53:44.120
Yeah,

53:44.680 --> 53:46.520
the Billy Boys are coming for you.

53:46.600 --> 53:47.440
How the fuck'd you find me?

53:49.480 --> 53:50.760
How the fuck did they find me?

53:50.840 --> 53:51.920
I kinda let it slip.

53:52.880 --> 53:54.040
Give you no choice.

53:54.720 --> 53:56.240
What? Hmm? What?

54:02.920 --> 54:03.760
No.

54:05.040 --> 54:07.160
In the Bentley outside,
the engine running.

54:07.240 --> 54:09.640
Fastest engine in the world apparently,
which is good.

54:10.240 --> 54:12.160
We got two minutes to get out of here.

54:31.440 --> 54:35.160
We are officers of
the East Lanarkshire Special Constabulary.

54:35.720 --> 54:38.760
We are seeking a man
by the name of Aberama Gold.

54:40.520 --> 54:42.440
Hand the gentleman over,

54:42.520 --> 54:44.520
and no one else will be harmed.

55:19.400 --> 55:20.560
Fuck! Take cover!

55:21.720 --> 55:22.600
[screaming]

55:45.640 --> 55:46.520
[grunting]

55:51.320 --> 55:52.840
[McCavern] So, Tommy Shelby.

55:52.920 --> 55:53.760
[sniffs]

55:54.840 --> 55:56.520
It's war you want...

55:59.000 --> 56:00.880
it's war you shall have.

56:15.720 --> 56:17.720
[theme song playing]

56:32.040 --> 56:36.080
♪ On a gathering storm
Comes a tall handsome man ♪

56:36.160 --> 56:40.760
♪ In a dusty black coat
With a red right hand ♪

56:48.520 --> 56:52.960
♪ A shadow is cast wherever he stands ♪

56:53.040 --> 56:57.160
♪ Stacks of green paper
In his red right hand ♪
